<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajyashri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajyashri was an Indian princess of the Pushyabhuti dynasty of Thanesar, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prabhakaravardhana">Prabhakaravardhana</a> and sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajyavardhana">Rajyavardhana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a>. Married to the Maukhari king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grahavarman">Grahavarman</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>, she was imprisoned after he was killed around 606 but escaped; according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banabhatta">Bana</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harshacharita">Harshacharita</a>, Harsha found her in the Vindhya forest as she was about to enter a fire. She later became a follower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>.</p></div>
